      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While gentle stretching may provide some relief, intense or heavy twisting can sometimes make the situation worse, as it can exacerbate the underlying injury or irritate the surrounding tissues. Additionally, if you have a serious spinal injury, pushing yourself to stretch or twist can worsening the damage. Consider trying over-the-counter pain relievers, such as ibuprofen or acetaminophen, and applying heat or cold packs to the area to help manage pain and inflammation. If your symptoms worsen or persist, it's still best to seek medical attention for a proper evaluation.",
